Solve a photograph and print the completed grid:
```bash
cdbr puzzle.heic
```

Print the recognised puzzle as TOML without solving it:
```bash
cdbr --orig puzzle.jpg
```

Review uncertain OCR cells and write the solution on the source photograph:
```bash
cdbr --review --image puzzle.heic
```

Write the solved photograph to an explicit path:
```bash
cdbr --image=finished.jpg puzzle.jpg
```

Create a themed puzzle with exactly three supplied clues:
```bash
cdbr create --include PERFECT --include PETERSFIELD --clues 3 \
    --output puzzle.toml --image puzzle.png
```

Search for better candidates for thirty minutes and retain every certified result:
```bash
cdbr create --include PERFECT --best-of 30 --max-candidates 30 \
    --output best.toml --image best.png --keep-candidates candidates
```

Run the local web application:
```bash
cdbrd --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```
